# Repository Agent Operating Contract

`AGENTS.md` is the canonical, host-neutral entry point for repository work. Host adapters may import it, but they do not replace its authority.

## Start here

1. Read [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md) for the knowledge and generated-surface map.
2. For substantive work, Main creates or resumes exactly one matching ordinary Markdown Plan in [`docs/exec-plans/active/`](docs/exec-plans/active/); setup itself never creates a Plan.
3. Read only the current authority, code, and tests named by that Plan or the local task.
4. Use the project-owned commands documented in [`docs/QUALITY.md`](docs/QUALITY.md) and [`docs/OPERATIONS.md`](docs/OPERATIONS.md).

When current sources conflict, stop and report the conflict. Do not silently choose the easiest interpretation.

After explicit setup handoff, this target is project-owned and independently useful. Package absence is expected and is not `UNKNOWN`, blocking, or a residual risk for ordinary target work. No generated target requires a package, runtime, role or procedure Skill, marker, generated settings, command wrapper, or hidden state. Reporivet does not execute project commands or spawn or dispatch Agents for this target.

